# The hooks projects bind through a shim.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT ARTIFACTS.
#
# ARTIFACTS declares what install-project-hooks.sh PUBLISHES to the shared bin
# directory. This file declares what projects BIND. They are different sets and
# the difference is not an oversight: openspec-change-gate is shimmed by every
# project, but its implementation is published by install-shared-artifact.sh
# alongside reviewer-cli and run-plan-review, so it has no row in this
# manifest's set. Merging the two lists would either make the installer publish
# an artifact it does not own or make the conformance scan blind to the gate —
# which is the shim carrying the §18 gate's only blocking condition.
#
# WHY IT IS DECLARED AT ALL.
#
# The retired conformance tool carried this set as a hardcoded array while the
# installer and the provisioning check read a declaration, so one fleet had two
# expected sets maintained in two places — the drift ARTIFACTS was created to
# prevent, reintroduced in a third tool (Stage-2 finding 7). `check-shims.sh`
# reads this file for the same reason.
#
# One hook name per line, without the .sh. Blank lines and # comments ignored.

database-sentinel
openspec-change-gate
